The correct answer is B. Ad hoc.

The question asks: Which wireless mode connects machines directly to one another without using an access point?

Let's explain all four options so you can understand them for your cybersecurity and networking exams.

### 1\. A. BSS (Basic Service Set)

![Topologies IEEE 802.11 - cisco.goffinet.org](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/ry5NPQLi7uMdO9gb1YkACiY4FL3_Ff0g5PqlT34i25c6dWVyJFDDIhguNy0JCpUUpApwOszR6Xznovak8LvIelCgDYwRP5kiZwwI1E_dtfHZMolFk3O2r6A-LL0XyS0f8lcU40j6yzJ7g7x6cJ_UJGQmuMRpG0DttszpWZDagh-R0PaMTg7OOIKFizVQ5ShU?purpose=fullsize)

* BSS is a group of wireless devices connected within one Wi-Fi network.

* In the traditional infrastructure BSS, devices communicate through a wireless access point (AP).

* The access point coordinates communication between devices.

* Example: Your phone and laptop connect to the same Wi-Fi router.

Remember: BSS = wireless network organized around an access point.

### 2\. B. Ad hoc

![PPT - Wireless Networks Security PowerPoint Presentation, free download - ID:70813](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/jpiBB1P-py5tH3fMXKKFlCvAqBQxeByvPQm726cgWQplhE12En9gzBBzipXjVTNZ25fcVM4zbhKEMXv3cTESycb80tuLdUIFpGfjlwwgi4hKstn8VTulTIzLXIAKuBXANioNS3UhsVL2FUdQVbYlsSdUxlTJea1dPpDyCSFp4pI07EYdH2s-KmacimHc4OVN?purpose=fullsize)

Correct answer

* Ad hoc is a wireless communication mode where devices connect directly to one another.

* It does not require a central access point or router.

* Devices communicate directly using wireless connections.

* Example: Two laptops connecting directly through a wireless ad hoc network.

Remember: Ad hoc = direct device-to-device communication without an access point.

### 3\. C. Infrastructure

