* Infrastructure mode uses an access point (AP) to manage wireless communication.

* Devices connect to the access point rather than forming a direct independent network.

* The access point can connect wireless devices to a wired network or the internet.

* Example: Your phone connects to your home Wi-Fi router.

Remember: Infrastructure = communication through an access point.

### 4\. D. Point to Point

![PPT - Is Wireless in Your Future? LAN’s, WAN’s, and Digital Canopies PowerPoint Presentation - ID:70827](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/vsoVTrmjTZt-khJRiHKdNDuNmIf7natDKtJJrKDyFMx3QvDnVA67PdnkouyCbp4koIIh3lnNFGsxOt2TFi1_X5gu2GDgvs9Q3txAmfMxsDQRo5KFb3Zdny4WM3OZMRIADTcJd9GfVLvmujgvsQutfxWfHKRTCK6yxsK4aM9KeIXDxXe3IURNIH9YtbO0_sLo?purpose=fullsize)

* Point-to-point describes a connection between two specific endpoints.

* It is commonly used to connect two buildings wirelessly.

* It can use directional antennas to establish a dedicated link.

* Example: Connecting two offices using wireless bridges.

Remember: Point-to-point = direct link between two endpoints.

